@firecraftgaming I thought this over and realized the goals we are trying to achieve are somewhat different. Your approach is oriented towards fixtures with different channel numbers, covering different regions, etc. My goal is essentially to output channel content onto a pixel matrix.

I ended up making a super stripped down version and called it pixel consumer. It has minimal processing and relies on the channel and mixer to do most of the heavy lifting. You can find it in #1751.

To use it, you define a custom channel resolution that matches dimensions of the pixel matrix and refresh rate. When you play an image or a video the channel will automatically re-scale the contents to fill the matrix. And you can use MIXER commands to display a sub-region and/or rotate it.

I am planning to add coefficients to account for different flux values for each color, and maybe "zig-zag" and "reverse" options to accommodate different wiring patterns (although most pixel controllers can do that already).

If you want, take a look and maybe we can figure out how to integrate them. I have a stiff deadline to get this thing into production, so I will have to focus on that.

@Julusian I'd be interested in hearing your opinion whether you think we should keep them separate to try to merge them into one.
