    Hmm, that seems to be a general limitation... @Julusian is there no way to add more than one instance of the same type of consumer to the same channel?

Consumers are 'deduplicated' based on the port number they assign themselves. which is pretty baked into the protocol in a way, as it allows for things like REMOVE 1 DECKLINK 3 to remove the correct thing.

I'm not sure how best to handle that for this artnet one, but it will need to assign itself a different number to allow multiple on a channel.

    My other thought was that if we keep it as a separate pixel consumer,

I dont think that is a problem with the current artnet name, we can either alias the name in the future, or leave it a little confusing but perhaps more descriptive in intention.

    I'd be interested in hearing your opinion whether you think we should keep them separate to try to merge them into one.

I think it would be good to try and combine them so that we have a clearer set of functionality (and less confusion about which to use). I havent read the above enough to get an idea on how viable that is, so do push back if it seems problematic



